# Compos Tutorial

Welcome to the Compos tutorial.

If you want to use AI, hold the META key (usually ALT or Option) and type x.
Then type setup-ai-guide and press Return. We write this as M-x setup-ai-guide.
That guide explains models, chats, agents, logins, and a first reply. You can
do the editor lessons below without a model. Return to the guide before the
Agents exercises.

This is your personal copy of the tutorial. Later we will tell you to change
it. Do not worry if you change it before we say so. That is called "editing",
and editing is what Compos is for.

You are reading one buffer. A buffer is a named place where Compos holds text:
a file, a chat, a help page, or this tutorial. This buffer is named TUTORIAL.
The cursor in the text is called point. Commands move point.

Compos commands involve the CONTROL key (often labelled CTRL or CTL) or the
META key (usually labelled ALT or Option). Instead of writing that in full
each time, we use these abbreviations:

  C-<chr>  Hold the CONTROL key while you type the character <chr>.
  M-<chr>  Hold the META or ALT key while you type <chr>.
  C-M-<chr>  Hold both CONTROL and META while you type <chr>.

You do not need to learn everything at once. Three commands make a wrong guess
easy to repair:

  C-g    Cancel the command or prompt you are in.
  M-x    Run a command by name.
  C-h t  Open or resume this tutorial.

C-h h (how-do-i) lists recipes for common tasks. C-h ? lists every help command.

The characters ">>" at the left margin mark directions for you to try. The
indented lines below them explain what to do. For example:

>> Type M-x to open the command prompt.
   Then type C-g to close it and return here.

